========================================================================
PART A — verify the W7 (+)_3 R = u(28)>=85 resonant product, exactly
========================================================================
  e(W7)=12, e(R)=5, |W7|=7, |R|=4
  ChordSpec(W7) = {1: 12, 3: 6, 4: 3}
  ChordSpec(R)  = {1: 5, 3: 1}
  shared chord norms ChordSpec(W7) & ChordSpec(R) = [1, 3]
  shared NON-unit (t>=2) norms = [3]   <-- the admissible resonant t

  generic product cap P(28) = e(W7)*|R| + |W7|*e(R) = 12*4 + 7*5 = 83
  3N = 84

   t= 3: loeschian=True   Delta_t=2  U= 85  >3N CROSS  <-- Moser sqrt(-11)
   t= 4: loeschian=True   Delta_t=0  U= 83  <3N
   t= 7: loeschian=True   Delta_t=0  U= 83  <3N
   t= 9: loeschian=True   Delta_t=0  U= 83  <3N
   t=12: loeschian=True   Delta_t=0  U= 83  <3N
   t=13: loeschian=True   Delta_t=0  U= 83  <3N

  ===> uniqueness check: Delta_t(R,W7) is NONZERO only for t in [3]  (scanned t=2..59)
  CONFIRMED: t=3 is the UNIQUE resonant norm for the R x W7 factorization.
  Reason: ChordSpec(R)={1,3}; R's only non-edge chord is sqrt3 (norm 3).
  And Delta_3 = 2 = the exact crossing 83 < 84 < 85.
